From 1140359c8692e068d8d60a7666302d58e7d0dc45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:31:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix slot collapse in start/sit, and diagnose a stale team id
 properly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three changes, all provoked by gladiator being discarded and rebuilt under
league id 115717708.

1. get_start_sit_slate built the current lineup as a dict keyed by
   slot_position. Every one of these leagues has two RB slots and two WR
   slots, so nine starters collapsed into seven, and the two that were
   dropped came back out of the set difference as "start these" — naming
   players already in the lineup. current_projected is summed from the
   roster directly, so the totals stayed correct and the bug survived a
   season of green tests. The tests added here assert on `changes`, and
   fail against the old code.

2. A team id that matches no team in the league reported "TEAM_ID not set
   in .env", sending you to check the one line that was fine. That is
   exactly what a league rebuild produces, since a recreated league hands
   out fresh team ids. The two states now say different things, and the
   error lists the league's teams so the replacement id is in the message.
   list_leagues previously noted only the unset case, so a stale id showed
   up as a league entry with no my_team key and no explanation.

   Worth stating what this cannot catch: team ids are small integers, so a
   stale id often collides with a real team in the new league. Then nothing
   errors and the advice describes a stranger's roster. The only defence is
   the team name, which list_leagues reports.

3. verify_leagues.py prints the teams and their ids whenever the configured
   team cannot be resolved, and prompts a name check when it can.

The skill's gladiator row is marked unverified rather than guessed at: the
rebuilt league's scoring did not necessarily carry over, so the bucketed
yardage rule is now a claim about a league that no longer exists. inai
corrected from 10 teams to 12.

No league id lives in this repo — they come from .env locally and fly
secrets in production, so the cutover itself is configuration, not code.

